matory physical findings", "Steroid-induced neuropathy: Possible but insufficient evidence to anchor as primary mechanism yet"], "alarm_features": ["17-pound weight loss (≥10% in 1 month)", "Chronic alcohol use", "Heavy tobacco use", "Steroid use", "Diabetes mellitus"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Central (Brain/Cord) Lesion", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.119, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Burning pain with subacute progression is inconsistent with typical cerebral infarction presentation."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Compressive Plexopathy / Apical Mass", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.095, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lack of Horner's syndrome weakly argues against apical lung tumor, which often presents with this autonomic sign."]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Peripheral Neuropathy / Radiculopathy", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.073, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Negative positional testing strengthens the central lesion hypothesis by differentiating it from cervical radiculopathy, which typically worsens with neck posi…"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Vascular (Subclavian Steal / Ischemia)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.7121122048442468, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Steroid use weakly supports vascular mechanisms through atherosclerosis risk, though direct evidence is limited."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of exertional symptoms and vascular signs provides moderate evidence against vascular etiologies."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B4.1", "B4.2", "B4.3", "B4.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification